{"step_index":137,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:07:05Z","input_tokens":3032,"cache_read_tokens":118029,"output_tokens":811,"content":"The CORS issue caused by opening the HTML files directly from the local file system (`file:///`) has been resolved.\n\n### Cause of the Issue\nWhen double-clicking an HTML file directly in Windows Explorer, browsers assign it an opaque origin of `'null'`. Under modern browser security rules, ES modules (`<script type=\"module\">`) are prohibited from importing other local files (`./firebase-config.js`), resulting in `net::ERR_FAILED` and CORS blockage.\n\n### Changes Applied\n1. **Dual-Mode CDN Scripts**:\n   - Replaced module-based imports in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) and [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) with the Google Firebase compat CDN scripts:\n     - `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app-compat.js`\n     - `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-firestore-compat.js`\n   - Inlined the Firebase configuration and Firestore operations.\n2. **Instant Rendering with Fallback Sync**:\n   - Synchronously initializes with default quiz data on load so the interface renders immediately without any network hang.\n   - Automatically synchronizes with Firestore in the background when connected to update with the teacher's published questions.\n3. **[HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md)**:\n   - Added Non-Major Patch 1.0.1 documenting the fix and rationale below the existing patch entry per Rule 1.\n4. **Zero In-Code Comments (Rule 9)**:\n   - Verified that zero comments, docstrings, or TODOs exist across all source files.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results (Rules 3 & 10)\n\n1. **Direct `file:///` Protocol Verification**:\n   - Tested [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) under `file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html` using headless Edge.\n   - Result: Renders `C Quiz: Switch Case`, 20 items, 20s timer rule, name/section inputs, and enabled \"Start Quiz\" button with **zero CORS errors**.\n   - Tested [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) under `file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html` using headless Edge.\n   - Result: Renders all 20 question cards with editable inputs, options panel, and \"+ Add Question\" button with **zero CORS errors**.\n2. **Vercel / HTTP Simulation**:\n   - Tested all files over local HTTP server; all returned HTTP status 200.\n3. **Firestore Connection**:\n   - Confirmed live read/write capability to `sir-jasper-quiz` Firestore collection `quizzes/active`.\n\nYou can now double-click either [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) or [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) directly in your browser or deploy this directory to Vercel."}
